    "https://mcdaniel.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205410": {
      "title": "American Sign Language (ASL) Tutor- Federal Work Study & Campus Employment",
      "description": "McDaniel College\nJob Posting: American Sign Language (ASL) Tutor- Federal Work Study & Campus Employment McDaniel College \n\tJob Posting: American Sign Language (ASL) Tutor- Federal Work Study & Campus Employment Title Home About Us Academics Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details American Sign Language (ASL) Tutor- Federal Work Study & Campus Employment Category: Student Worker Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: American Sign Language Locations: Westminster, MD Posted: Oct 1, 2026 Closes: Nov 12, 2026 - 11:59 PM EST Type: PT No Benefits Salary Type: Hourly Salary Range: $15.00 - $15.00 Position ID: 205410 Share About McDaniel College: McDaniel College is a four-year, independent college of the liberal arts and sciences offering over 100 undergraduate and graduate programs. One of the original \"Colleges That Change Lives,\" McDaniel emphasizes experiential learning and student-faculty collaboration to develop the unique potential in every student. Represented by the Green Terror, over 20 athletic teams compete in the NCAA Division III Centennial Conference. A student-centered community of 1,600 undergraduates and 1,400 graduate students offers access to both Baltimore and Washington, D.C., plus a European campus in Budapest, Hungary. At McDaniel College we value our employees by offering our full-time employees tuition remission, 403B retirement accounts, paid time off, medical insurance, flexible spending accounts, life insurance, and paid maternity and parental leave. For more information about the college's benefits, please click here to review the 2026 benefits guidebook and click here to view 2026 premium rates . Click here to see how McDaniel College employees impact the lives of students. Job Description: Position: American Sign Language (ASL) Tutor Reports to: ASL Studies Staff/Faculty ASL Studies Program Assistant ASL Studies Lab Manager ASL Studies Interim Department Chair Department: ASL Studies Salary Grade: Maryland Minimum Wage FSLA Status: Non-exempt Location:  McDaniel College, 2 College Hill, Westminster, MD 21157 Duration of Appointment: August 5, 2026 to May 25, 2027 Schedule: Schedule is at discretion of supervisor Evaluation Procedures: Student workers are evaluated on a continuing basis Scope: The American Sign Language (ASL) Tutor will provide aid to undergraduate students learning the material for ASL 1, ASL 2, ASL 3 and ASL 4 classes to undergraduate students enrolled in ASL classes at McDaniel College. Responsibilities: Meet with one to four students per session, based on the ASL Tutoring sign-up schedule. Document attendance and provide brief notes for the ASL instructor as to how the student performed during the tutoring time. Comments will include areas of strength and areas for improvement. Provide a highly personal and very interactive environment in which undergraduates can experience a positive encounter with a tutor while improving upon learned ASL skills. Requirements: Current McDaniel undergraduate student Must have completed ASL 1, ASL 2, ASL 3, and ASL 4 with B+ or higher GPA Familiar with the Signing Naturally curriculum implemented by the department Demonstrate competency in the structure of ASL and its grammatical rules Have flexibility to tutor students at different levels (ASL 1 - 4) Document attendance of students receiving tutoring Correspond with instructor (cc: ASL Lab Coordinator) date and time of tutoring session, including what skills were worked on. Additional Information: McDaniel College, in compliance with federal and state laws and regulations, does not discriminate in the recruitment, admission, and employment of students, faculty, and staff in the operation of any of its educational programs and activities. McDaniel College will not tolerate any discrimination or harassment on the basis of any protected status including protective hairstyle, race, religion, color, ancestry or national origin, disability, age, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, pregnancy, military status, genetic information, marital status, veteran's status, or any other actual or perceived legally protected characteristics. Application Instructions: Please click the Apply Now button below to begin your application. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation McDaniel College 2 College Hill Westminster, MD, 21157"
