    "https://mcdaniel.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205111": {
      "title": "Boys & Girls Club- Mentor (Youth Development Professional)",
      "description": "McDaniel College\nJob Posting: Boys & Girls Club- Mentor (Youth Development Professional) McDaniel College \n\tJob Posting: Boys & Girls Club- Mentor (Youth Development Professional) Title Home About Us Academics Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Boys & Girls Club- Mentor (Youth Development Professional) Category: Student Worker Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Center for Experience and Oppo Locations: Westminster, MD Posted: Sep 23, 2026 Closes: Nov 4, 2026 - 11:59 PM EST Type: PT No Benefits Salary Type: Hourly Salary Range: $15.00 - $15.00 Position ID: 205111 Share About McDaniel College: McDaniel College is a four-year, independent college of the liberal arts and sciences offering over 100 undergraduate and graduate programs. One of the original \"Colleges That Change Lives,\" McDaniel emphasizes experiential learning and student-faculty collaboration to develop the unique potential in every student. Represented by the Green Terror, over 20 athletic teams compete in the NCAA Division III Centennial Conference. A student-centered community of 1,600 undergraduates and 1,400 graduate students offers access to both Baltimore and Washington, D.C., plus a European campus in Budapest, Hungary. At McDaniel College we value our employees by offering our full-time employees tuition remission, 403B retirement accounts, paid time off, medical insurance, flexible spending accounts, life insurance, and paid maternity and parental leave. For more information about the college's benefits, please click here to review the 2026 benefits guidebook and click here to view 2026 premium rates . Click here to see how McDaniel College employees impact the lives of students. Job Description: Job Title: Boys & Girls Club- Mentor (Youth Development Professional) Effective Date: 08/09/2026 Reports to: Senior Program Director Department: Center for Experience & Opportunity Rate of Pay: Maryland Minimum Wage FSLA Status: Non-Exempt Location of Position: Boys & Girls Club of Westminster, 71 East Main Street, Westminster, MD 21157 Duration of Appointment: August 5, 2026 to May 25, 2027 Schedule: Schedule is at discretion of supervisor Evaluation Procedures: Student workers are evaluated on a continuous basis. Scope: Mentors provide direct supervision, positive engagement, and program support for Boys & Girls Club members. Mentors are expected to actively and enthusiastically engage with members, manage behavior, maintain safety, support scheduled programs, and clean and reset their assigned spaces. Responsibilities: Attend the daily shift meetings before reporting to an assignment. Mentors who drive separately or arrive after the meeting must check in with a Director before beginning work. Review the daily schedule, assigned placement, programs, visitors, special events, and relevant member information. Report to the assigned space and remain there unless reassigned or a Director has arranged coverage. Maintain active supervision and remain attentive at all times; do not sit on the sidelines, use a personal cell phone, or become distracted while members are present. Actively engage members through games, conversations, homework support, Club materials, technology, and other appropriate activities. Lead assigned clubs or planned activities and support programs led by staff, volunteers, donors, and community partners. Monitor member interactions, technology use, treatment of property, and participation in required homework or program activities to ensure expectations are followed. Use positive reinforcement techniques, coaching, and trauma-informed practices to promote a safe, positive, and inclusive environment. Intervene promptly and consistently when behavior is unsafe, disrespectful, or disruptive, and contact a Director when it is repeated, escalating, or unsafe. Promptly report member concerns, behavior patterns, safety issues, or requests for support to a Director. Follow all movement, safety, and in-Club communication procedures, including supervising member transitions and avoiding one-on-one situations. Maintain professional boundaries and confidentiality. Do not communicate with, transport, tutor, coach, or connect with members or their families outside of Club-approved activities. Communicate professionally with Club leadership, ask for support when needed, and accept direction, coaching, and feedback. Attend all required trainings throughout the school year. Before leaving, sweep or vacuum, wipe surfaces, return materials, remove trash, and reset the assigned space. Call a Director to inspect and approve the space, then assist with remaining tasks as directed. Schedule: Shifts are available Monday through Friday, from 2:00PM - 6:00PM or 3:00PM - 6:00PM (Based on availability and program needs). Mentors may work one or more consistent days each week based on their class schedule, Federal Work Study award, and Club staffing needs. Mentors must reliably attend assigned shifts. Call-outs must be reported to the front desk by 12:00PM; lateness must be reported as soon as the delay is known. Transportation from McDaniel College may be provided for scheduled shifts, but is not guaranteed. Mentors may also drive themselves. Requirements: Qualifications: Current undergraduate student at McDaniel College. Eligible for Federal Work Study as part of a Financial Aid Package. Dependable, punctual, and able to communicate questions, concerns, and schedule changes directly and professionally. High-energy, positive, and enthusiastic, with the ability and willingness to work in a fast-paced youth-development environment. Ability to actively supervise, engage, and redirect groups of children and teenagers. Ability to maintain professional boundaries, confidentiality, and appropriate role-modeling behavior. Willingness to lead activities, clean assigned spaces, work as part of a team, and accept coaching. Preferred Qualifications: Previous experience mentoring, working, or volunteering with children or teenagers. Experience leading games, clubs, sports, arts, academic support, or other group activities. Interest in education, social work, psychology, recreation, youth development, or a related field. Additional Information: McDaniel College, in compliance with federal and state laws and regulations, does not discriminate in the recruitment, admission, and employment of students, faculty, and staff in the operation of any of its educational programs and activities. McDaniel College will not tolerate any discrimination or harassment on the basis of any protected status including protective hairstyle, race, religion, color, ancestry or national origin, disability, age, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, pregnancy, military status, genetic information, marital status, veteran's status, or any other actual or perceived legally protected characteristics. Application Instructions: Please click the Apply Now button below to begin your application. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation McDaniel College 2 College Hill Westminster, MD, 21157"
    },
    "https://mcdaniel.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204805": {
      "title": "Support Services Clerk - Delivery Assistant- Federal Work Study Only",
      "description": "McDaniel College\nJob Posting: Support Services Clerk - Delivery Assistant- Federal Work Study Only McDaniel College \n\tJob Posting: Support Services Clerk - Delivery Assistant- Federal Work Study Only Title Home About Us Academics Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Support Services Clerk - Delivery Assistant- Federal Work Study Only Category: Student Worker Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Post Office Locations: Westminster, MD Posted: Sep 21, 2026 Closes: Nov 2, 2026 - 11:59 PM EST Type: PT No Benefits Salary Type: Hourly Salary Range: $15.00 - $15.00 Position ID: 204805 Share About McDaniel College: McDaniel College is a four-year, independent college of the liberal arts and sciences offering over 100 undergraduate and graduate programs. One of the original \"Colleges That Change Lives,\" McDaniel emphasizes experiential learning and student-faculty collaboration to develop the unique potential in every student. Represented by the Green Terror, over 20 athletic teams compete in the NCAA Division III Centennial Conference. A student-centered community of 1,600 undergraduates and 1,400 graduate students offers access to both Baltimore and Washington, D.C., plus a European campus in Budapest, Hungary. At McDaniel College we value our employees by offering our full-time employees tuition remission, 403B retirement accounts, paid time off, medical insurance, flexible spending accounts, life insurance, and paid maternity and parental leave. For more information about the college's benefits, please click here to review the 2026 benefits guidebook and click here to view 2026 premium rates . Click here to see how McDaniel College employees impact the lives of students. Job Description: Job Title: Support Services Clerk - Delivery Assistant Effective Date: 08/27/2026 Reports to: Assistant Director of Auxiliary Services Department: Post Office Rate of Pay: Maryland Minimum Wage FSLA Status: Non-Exempt Location of Position: Roj Student Center, McDaniel College, 2 College Hill, Westminster, MD 21157 Duration of Appointment: August 5, 2026 - May 25, 2027 Schedule: Schedule is at discretion of supervisor Evaluation Procedures: Student workers are evaluated on a continuous basis. Scope: Responsible for working in the Copy Center and Post Office to provide mail distribution and quality copying to the college community. Hours will vary based on scheduling and staffing needs during normal college business hours, Monday - Friday. RESPONSIBILITIES- Basic Responsibilities Oversee the delivery and receiving of USPS mail and packages, FedEx, UPS packages, all other carriers' packages, and Copy Center printing. Participate in maintaining an efficient Post Office and Copy Center by performing all duties pertaining to each department. Establish a reputation among campus customers for performing duties efficiently and courteously and for forming an excellent working relationship with the employees of the Post Office and Copy Center. Prioritize and maintain the quality and timeliness of the Post Office and Copy Center service. Maintain an inventory and distribution of office supplies, mailing supplies and stamps. Specific Responsibilities Performs all duties pertaining to the Post Office Follow and interpret official US postal regulations and guidelines. Sort, distribute, forward, and deliver USPS and inter-campus departmental mail. Process and meter outgoing USPS mail. Provide courteous window service while selling USPS products/services, mailing supplies, and faxes. Send and receive faxes. Deliver mail, packages, and print jobs to the college community in a timely manner. Operate computerized mail-metering machine, fax machine, and USPS weight scale, and all other equipment necessary to perform duties. Maintain a balanced cash drawer. Log and distribute packages to the college community. Process incoming business reply mail. Handle and process bulk mailings. Complete necessary bulk mailing forms. Perform all other duties as assigned. Performs all duties pertaining to the Copy Center Operate copiers, folder, laminator, paper cutter, poster printer, binder, and all other machinery pertaining to the Copy Center. Develop the knowledge and skills to effectively operate and maintain the Copy Center equipment with on-the-job training. Complete all printing requests on time by prioritizing the due dates and time. Disburse office supply requests and assist with maintaining the inventory and ordering of stock. Maintain courteous customer service skills and communication with supervisor and co-workers. Perform all other duties as assigned. Requirements: Qualifications: Current undergraduate student at McDaniel College. Must be eligible for Federal Work Study as part of a financial aid package. The ability to stand for long periods of time. Must be able to lift 60 pounds. Good interpersonal and customer service skills. Good oral and written communication skills. Good organizational skills. The ability to perform multiple duties and respond to short notices. Must be computer proficient. Physical Characteristics: This position requires standing for long periods of time as well as bending and stooping. This position does require the ability to lift up to 60 pounds. This position requires the ability to deliver mail throughout campus on foot during all types of weather and adverse conditions. Additional Information: McDaniel College, in compliance with federal and state laws and regulations, does not discriminate in the recruitment, admission, and employment of students, faculty, and staff in the operation of any of its educational programs and activities. McDaniel College will not tolerate any discrimination or harassment on the basis of any protected status including protective hairstyle, race, religion, color, ancestry or national origin, disability, age, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, pregnancy, military status, genetic information, marital status, veteran's status, or any other actual or perceived legally protected characteristics. Application Instructions: Please click the Apply Now button below to begin your application. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation McDaniel College 2 College Hill Westminster, MD, 21157"
