    "https://mcdaniel.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205505": {
      "title": "Academic Secretary",
      "description": "McDaniel College\nJob Posting: Academic Secretary McDaniel College \n\tJob Posting: Academic Secretary Title Home About Us Academics Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Academic Secretary Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Nursing Locations: Westminster, MD Posted: Oct 5, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Salary Type: Hourly Salary Range: $17.25 - $17.25 Position ID: 205505 Share About McDaniel College: McDaniel College is a four-year, independent college of the liberal arts and sciences offering over 100 undergraduate and graduate programs. One of the original \"Colleges That Change Lives,\" McDaniel emphasizes experiential learning and student-faculty collaboration to develop the unique potential in every student. Represented by the Green Terror, over 20 athletic teams compete in the NCAA Division III Centennial Conference. A student-centered community of 1,600 undergraduates and 1,400 graduate students offers access to both Baltimore and Washington, D.C., plus a European campus in Budapest, Hungary. This position has a budgeted hiring rate of $17.25/hr. The position is classified as a C3. Positions in the C3 salary band have a minimum rate of $16.75/hr and a maximum rate of $24.12/hr. At McDaniel College we value our employees by offering our full-time employees tuition remission, 403B retirement accounts, paid time off, medical insurance, flexible spending accounts, life insurance, and paid maternity and parental leave. For more information about the college's benefits, please click here to review the 2026 benefits guidebook and click here to view 2026 premium rates . Click here to see how McDaniel College employees impact the lives of students. Job Description: Provides administrative and secretarial support to the Department of Nursing Chair and other members of the Department of Nursing as assigned. Key Responsibilities The Academic Secretary provides comprehensive administrative and operational support to the Department of Nursing Chair. This support includes calendar and meeting management, correspondence, departmental communications, committee support, event coordination, and confidential matters. This role supports day-to-day department operations by coordinating budgets, invoices, contracts, purchasing, facilities, room scheduling, supplies, technology and inventory, and office coverage. This position assists with student admissions, onboarding, academic integrity processes, faculty and staff recruitment and onboarding, course scheduling, textbook procurement, and departmental records. The Academic Secretary coordinates accreditation, program review, assessment, and regulatory activities by administering surveys, collecting and compiling data, maintaining documentation, preparing reports, and organizing accreditation visits and related initiatives. The role maintains departmental websites and portal pages, supports faculty and student communications, facilitates collaboration across college departments, and provides administrative support for educational programs, orientations, meetings, retreats, and other departmental events. Requirements: High school graduate with two years college preferred; experience may be substituted for college. Experience in an office environment as an administrative assistant. Past experience working in higher education is desirable. Excellent organizational skills, detail oriented and ability to multi-task and be effective under pressure in a fast-paced environment. Competent in computer word processing, database, and spreadsheets. Excellent interpersonal skills are essential. Ability to exercise discretion in dealing with sensitive information. Integrity and good judgment. Ability to function in a fast-paced dynamic environment is a must Good written and oral skills. Additional Information: McDaniel College, in compliance with federal and state laws and regulations, does not discriminate in the recruitment, admission, and employment of students, faculty, and staff in the operation of any of its educational programs and activities. McDaniel College will not tolerate any discrimination or harassment on the basis of any protected status including protective hairstyle, race, religion, color, ancestry or national origin, disability, age, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, pregnancy, military status, genetic information, marital status, veteran's status, or any other actual or perceived legally protected characteristics. Application Instructions: To apply For a complete job description including essential responsibilities and to apply, please visit the college's employment webpage. Completed applications must include a cover letter addressing position qualifications and related experience, resume, and the names and contact information of three professional references. Review of applications will begin immediately. The position will be open until filled. Please click the Apply Now button below to begin your application. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation McDaniel College 2 College Hill Westminster, MD, 21157"
    },
    "https://mcdaniel.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204356": {
      "title": "Building Maintenance Mechanic- Lead HVAC/R Technician",
      "description": "McDaniel College\nJob Posting: Building Maintenance Mechanic- Lead HVAC/R Technician McDaniel College \n\tJob Posting: Building Maintenance Mechanic- Lead HVAC/R Technician Title Home About Us Academics Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Building Maintenance Mechanic- Lead HVAC/R Technician Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Physical Plant Locations: Westminster, MD Posted: Sep 1, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Salary Type: Hourly Salary Range: $45.00 - $45.00 Position ID: 204356 Share About McDaniel College: McDaniel College is a four-year, independent college of the liberal arts and sciences offering over 100 undergraduate and graduate programs. One of the original \"Colleges That Change Lives,\" McDaniel emphasizes experiential learning and student-faculty collaboration to develop the unique potential in every student. Represented by the Green Terror, over 20 athletic teams compete in the NCAA Division III Centennial Conference. A student-centered community of 1,600 undergraduates and 1,400 graduate students offers access to both Baltimore and Washington, D.C., plus a European campus in Budapest, Hungary. This position has a budgeted hiring rate of $45.00/hr. The position is classified as a S7. The S7 salary band for all full-time, 12-month positions at the college with this classification have a minimum rate of $25/hr and a maximum rate of $47.50/hr. At McDaniel College we value our employees by offering our full-time employees tuition remission, 403B retirement accounts, paid time off, medical insurance, flexible spending accounts, life insurance, and paid maternity and parental leave. For more information about the college's benefits, please click here to review the 2026 benefits guidebook and click here to view 2026 premium rates . Click here to see how McDaniel College employees impact the lives of students. Job Description: This is a hands-on position responsible for the maintenance and repair of all College heating, ventilating, air conditioning, refrigeration (HVAC), air quality equipment (including energy recovery make-up, exhausted air systems, and laboratory vent/chemical storage hoods).  Performs duties that may be outside of the HVAC trade to support priorities of the Physical Plant. This position is classified as essential meaning employee must report when college is closed. Occasional overtime and on-call responsibilities is required. Key Responsibilities The following are typical examples of the type of work performed under this job description. This list does not include all work to be performed and duties are subject to change as deemed necessary by the Director of Building Operations and Maintenance. Assist Director Building Operations and Maintenance to develop on going preventive maintenance program. Perform routine and preventive maintenance on air conditioners, air handlers, fan coil units, grease motors/bearings/pumps, change filters and belts, calibrate stats, clean condenser and evaporator coils, fume hood and exhaust fans, cooling towers, etc.  Perform duties such as grease motors/bearings/pumps, change filters and belts, calibrate stats, clean condenser and evaporator coils, etc. Work on rooftop units, split systems, VAV systems, heat pumps, geothermal systems, HVAC controls and related mechanical equipment. Make necessary repairs or replacements to bearings, fans, motors, actuators, controllers, pumps, refrigeration equipment etc. Use automated control systems to monitor and control building temperature. Action taken in the automated system shall not take the place of making a repair. Works with Director of Building Operations and Maintenance to provide information for ordering supplies and materials or directly orders supplies and materials as requested. Perform minor electrical work such as replacing fuses, receptacles, switches, contactors, resetting breakers, etc. Make adjustments to controls, thermostats, timers, etc. Ensures seasonal changeover of equipment is done properly and on time. Trains HVAC technicians in safety practices, procedures, and proper usage of equipment. Perform chemical testing of cooling towers and take appropriate action based on test results. Coordinate with outside contractor to perform contractual duties to chillers and cooling towers.  Periodically make repairs such as:  replace floats, clean/replace sump pump strainers, replace pumps, etc. Clean equipment in related areas.  Keep mechanical rooms and work areas clean. Complete work orders in a timely fashion and make daily updates when work has been performed. Work as part of the maintenance team to perform group projects such as but not limited to:  Installation/cleaning/removal window air conditioners, Stage set ups, Turnover of residential buildings for summer conferences, ready buildings for student return, etc.  There could be limited time off and working hours are subject to change according to the College's schedule. Perform maintenance and repairs of a general nature as requested. Perform snow removal. Operate, maintain, and use in a safe manner College equipment, tools, and vehicles. Regular and predictable attendance is required. Other duties as assigned. Requirements: Must demonstrate skill and experience equivalent to a minimum of three to five years' experience in commercial/residential HVACR with at least one year of supervisory experience preferred. Refrigeration Transition and Recovery Universal Certification is required along with 2L training preferred. Current Maryland Journeyman or Master HVAC License required and must be maintained. Master License is preferred. Must have valid driver's license with two or less points. Must be able to work during emergency weather events including but not limited to snow, hurricanes, tornados, etc. Must be able to respond to campus emergencies when called. Must have the ability to read and comprehend written instructions, procedures, and service manuals. Must have the ability to express oneself orally as well as in writing. Must have the ability to learn departmental policies, procedures, and mechanical systems, proper use of tools and materials used to perform duties within a ninety-day probationary period. Must be able to wear a respirator (i.e., N95), with required medical evaluation and annual fit testing. Additional Information: McDaniel College, in compliance with federal and state laws and regulations, does not discriminate in the recruitment, admission, and employment of students, faculty, and staff in the operation of any of its educational programs and activities. McDaniel College will not tolerate any discrimination or harassment on the basis of any protected status including protective hairstyle, race, religion, color, ancestry or national origin, disability, age, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, pregnancy, military status, genetic information, marital status, veteran's status, or any other actual or perceived legally protected characteristics. Application Instructions: To apply For a complete job description including essential responsibilities and to apply, please visit the college's employment webpage. Completed applications must include a cover letter addressing position qualifications and related experience, resume, and the names and contact information of three professional references. Review of applications will begin immediately. The position will be open until filled. Please click the Apply Now button below to begin your application. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation McDaniel College 2 College Hill Westminster, MD, 21157"
    },
    "https://mcdaniel.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204381": {
      "title": "Director of Annual Giving",
      "description": "McDaniel College\nJob Posting: Director of Annual Giving McDaniel College \n\tJob Posting: Director of Annual Giving Title Home About Us Academics Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Director of Annual Giving Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Annual Giving Locations: Westminster, MD Posted: Sep 2, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $90,000.00 - $90,000.00 Position ID: 204381 Share About McDaniel College: McDaniel College is a four-year, independent college of the liberal arts and sciences offering over 100 undergraduate and graduate programs. One of the original \"Colleges That Change Lives,\" McDaniel emphasizes experiential learning and student-faculty collaboration to develop the unique potential in every student. Represented by the Green Terror, over 20 athletic teams compete in the NCAA Division III Centennial Conference. A student-centered community of 1,600 undergraduates and 1,400 graduate students offers access to both Baltimore and Washington, D.C., plus a European campus in Budapest, Hungary. This position has a budgeted hiring rate of $90,000. The position is classified as an A5. The A5 salary band for all full-time, 12-month positions at the college with this classification have a minimum rate of $60,000 and a maximum rate of $135,000. The actual schedule for exempt positions may vary based on the workload and responsibilities assigned. At McDaniel College we value our employees by offering our full-time employees tuition remission, 403B retirement accounts, paid time off, medical insurance, flexible spending accounts, life insurance, and paid maternity and parental leave. For more information about the college's benefits, please click here to review the 2026 benefits guidebook and click here to view 2026 premium rates . Click here to see how McDaniel College employees impact the lives of students. Job Description: Reporting to the Vice President for Institutional Advancement, the Director of Annual Giving oversees the design and execution of McDaniel College's annual giving program to raise at least $2 million in annual gifts from its more than 23,000 alumni and friends. The Director leads a  three-person team to cultivate, solicit, and steward annual giving donors ($1 - $24,999).  The Director works closely with the Alumni Engagement and Advancement Services teams in using technology, social media, and research to design and implement strategies to increase giving at all levels as part of the college's public phase of the Reaching New Heights campaign. The Director of Annual Giving will carry a portfolio of 75-125 prospects. The position is expected to personally raise $200,000-$400,000 in new cash and pledges annually through annual and major gifts. The Director of Annual Giving will open 6-12 new proposals ($10,000 or more) and close 5-10 proposals ($10,000 or more) per year. To accomplish these metrics, the position will make at least 100 visits with donors and prospects each year. The Director serves on the Institutional Advancement leadership team. Key Responsibilities The Director of Annual Giving provides strategic leadership for McDaniel College's annual fundraising efforts, managing a team of two staff members and overseeing a comprehensive, multi-channel annual giving program designed to raise $2 million annually. The role is responsible for cultivating and soliciting donors through personalized campaigns, reunion giving programs, athletic fundraising initiatives, and college-wide giving days, while creating engagement opportunities tied to alumni and donor affiliations. The Director maintains a portfolio of 75-125 prospects, conducts at least 100 donor visits each year, and partners closely with development officers to identify, cultivate, and secure major gift opportunities. Additional responsibilities include analyzing fundraising performance data, developing dashboards and projections, managing departmental budgets, collaborating with Communications and Marketing to ensure brand consistency, supporting divisional events and initiatives, supervising for two annual giving positions, serving on the Institutional Advancement leadership team, and maintaining flexibility for travel and evening or weekend engagement activities. Requirements: Bachelor's degree required. Five to seven years of demonstrated annual giving experience and success at a non-profit organization, preferably in a higher education setting, required. Demonstrated success in the personal cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship of annual giving donors required. Ability to work independently as well as within a team environment to achieve institutional goals. Strong analytical and independent decision-making capability required. Demonstrated supervisory and budgetary experience required. Excellent written and oral communications skills required. Strong project management, leadership, organizational planning skills with the ability to set priorities and balance concurrent tasks. The ability to recruit, motivate, and direct alumni and parent volunteers. Proficiency in customer relations management database systems; preferably Slate and/or Blackbaud Raiser's Edge/NXT. Proficiency in online giving platforms such as GiveCampus or Slate preferred. Experience with the use of texting, social media, online giving platforms, and crowdfunding in annual giving solicitations required. Flexible and available for evening, weekend, or early morning events and meetings. Ability to travel as needed to manage a prospect portfolio. Must possess a valid driver's license with two or less points. Additional Information: McDaniel College, in compliance with federal and state laws and regulations, does not discriminate in the recruitment, admission, and employment of students, faculty, and staff in the operation of any of its educational programs and activities. McDaniel College will not tolerate any discrimination or harassment on the basis of any protected status including protective hairstyle, race, religion, color, ancestry or national origin, disability, age, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, pregnancy, military status, genetic information, marital status, veteran's status, or any other actual or perceived legally protected characteristics. Application Instructions: To apply For a complete job description including essential responsibilities and to apply, please visit the college's employment webpage. Completed applications must include a cover letter addressing position qualifications and related experience, resume, and the names and contact information of three professional references. Review of applications will begin immediately. The position will be open until filled. Please click the Apply Now button below to begin your application. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation McDaniel College 2 College Hill Westminster, MD, 21157"
    },
    "https://mcdaniel.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205659": {
      "title": "Payroll Specialist",
      "description": "McDaniel College\nJob Posting: Payroll Specialist McDaniel College \n\tJob Posting: Payroll Specialist Title Home About Us Academics Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Payroll Specialist Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Human Resources Locations: Westminster, MD Posted: Oct 9, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $61,000.00 - $61,000.00 Position ID: 205659 Share About McDaniel College: McDaniel College is a four-year, independent college of the liberal arts and sciences offering over 100 undergraduate and graduate programs. One of the original \"Colleges That Change Lives,\" McDaniel emphasizes experiential learning and student-faculty collaboration to develop the unique potential in every student. Represented by the Green Terror, over 20 athletic teams compete in the NCAA Division III Centennial Conference. A student-centered community of 1,600 undergraduates and 1,400 graduate students offers access to both Baltimore and Washington, D.C., plus a European campus in Budapest, Hungary. This position has a budgeted hiring rate of $61,000. The position is classified as an A4. The A4 salary band for all full-time, 12-month positions at the college with this classification have a minimum rate of $50,000 and a maximum rate of $93,780. The actual schedule for exempt positions may vary based on the workload and responsibilities assigned. This is an on-site working position. At McDaniel College we value our employees by offering our full-time employees tuition remission, 403B retirement accounts, paid time off, medical insurance, flexible spending accounts, life insurance, and paid maternity and parental leave. For more information about the college's benefits, please click here to review the 2026 benefits guidebook and click here to view 2026 premium rates . Click here to see how McDaniel College employees impact the lives of students. Job Description: The Payroll Specialist independently coordinates the College's payroll operations and is accountable for the accuracy, timeliness, compliance, and integrity of each payroll cycle. The position reviews employee and payroll data, resolves discrepancies, administers pay adjustments, maintains payroll records, and produces reports supporting institutional decision-making and regulatory compliance. Working in collaboration with Human Resources, Budget, and Financial Aid, the Payroll Specialist exercises judgment in evaluating payroll information, identifying issues, and determining appropriate action within established policies and applicable federal, state, and local requirements. Key Responsibilities The Payroll Specialist is responsible for the accurate and timely processing of payroll for faculty, staff, and student employees while ensuring compliance with College policies and federal, state, and local regulations. Key responsibilities include: Process and reconcile payroll, including timesheets, manual checks, stop payments, stipends, garnishments, leave accruals, and related transactions. Maintain accurate employee and payroll records in ADP Workforce Now, including new hires, compensation changes, tax elections, direct deposits, and separations. Analyze payroll and financial reports, resolve discrepancies, prepare journal entries, and maintain supporting payroll documentation. Ensure employee data remains accurate and aligned between ADP Workforce Now and Colleague, including importing and exporting data and identifying opportunities to improve system efficiencies. Partner with HR, Benefits, Financial Aid, and other departments on benefits transactions, FMLA, work-study earnings, W-2/1095 preparation, and other payroll-related matters. Serve as a resource to faculty, staff, students, supervisors, and external agencies by responding to payroll questions and resolving issues in a timely and professional manner. Maintain confidentiality of sensitive employee and payroll information while consistently meeting established payroll deadlines. Stay current on payroll regulations, ADP updates, and industry practices to support compliance and continuous process improvement. Requirements: Associate's degree or equivalent experience required, Bachelors degree preferred. Three or more years of related experience. Proficient financial knowledge to calculate payroll and produce journal entries. Experience with HRIS systems required, ADP payroll processing and Colleague software preferred. Must be able to understand and apply local, state and federal employment regulations Competent writing skills including excellent grammar, spelling, and punctuation Ability to accurately assess and handle phone calls, visitor requests, etc., with discretion and a positive attitude Ability to prioritize duties and work independently. Intermediate computer skills (database, Internet, email, MS office) Excellent organizational skills Ability to deal with complex situations  while maintaining the decorum of the Human Resource Office Must be able to anticipate and plan for cyclical activities. Discretion and reliability in sensitive and confidential matters are vital Additional Information: McDaniel College, in compliance with federal and state laws and regulations, does not discriminate in the recruitment, admission, and employment of students, faculty, and staff in the operation of any of its educational programs and activities. McDaniel College will not tolerate any discrimination or harassment on the basis of any protected status including protective hairstyle, race, religion, color, ancestry or national origin, disability, age, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, pregnancy, military status, genetic information, marital status, veteran's status, or any other actual or perceived legally protected characteristics. Application Instructions: To apply For a complete job description including essential responsibilities and to apply, please visit the college's employment webpage. Completed applications must include a cover letter addressing position qualifications and related experience, resume, and the names and contact information of three professional references. Review of applications will begin immediately. The position will be open until filled. Please click the Apply Now button below to begin your application. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation McDaniel College 2 College Hill Westminster, MD, 21157"
