    "https://mcdaniel.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203387": {
      "title": "Shuttle Driver",
      "description": "McDaniel College\nJob Posting: Shuttle Driver McDaniel College \n\tJob Posting: Shuttle Driver Title Home About Us Academics Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Shuttle Driver Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Campus Safety Locations: Westminster, MD Posted: Aug 5, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Salary Type: Hourly Salary Range: $18.00 - $18.00 Position ID: 203387 Share About McDaniel College: McDaniel College is a four-year, independent college of the liberal arts and sciences offering over 100 undergraduate and graduate programs. One of the original \"Colleges That Change Lives,\" McDaniel emphasizes experiential learning and student-faculty collaboration to develop the unique potential in every student. Represented by the Green Terror, over 20 athletic teams compete in the NCAA Division III Centennial Conference. A student-centered community of 1,600 undergraduates and 1,400 graduate students offers access to both Baltimore and Washington, D.C., plus a European campus in Budapest, Hungary. This position has a budgeted hiring rate of $18.00/hr. The position is classified as an S4. The S4 salary band for all part-time, hourly positions at the college with this classification have a minimum rate of $15.25/hr and a maximum rate of $21.50/hr. This is a part-time, 10-month position. At McDaniel College we value our employees by offering our full-time employees tuition remission, 403B retirement accounts, paid time off, medical insurance, flexible spending accounts, life insurance, and paid maternity and parental leave. For more information about the college's benefits, please click here to review the 2026 benefits guidebook and click here to view 2026 premium rates . Click here to see how McDaniel College employees impact the lives of students. Job Description: Reporting to the Support Services Manager, the Shuttle Driver is to transport student passengers to and from locations using a campus vehicle.  Daily Shuttle locations include the College campus and other businesses and medical facilities in the Westminster area. Break Shuttle locations include BWI Airport and BWI Amtrak. Key Responsibilities Follow all State, Local, and Federal Traffic laws while in McDaniel vehicles. Adhere to guidelines and regulations as they pertain to the College Driving Policy. Daily Shuttle responsibilities consist of transporting student passengers in an 11-passenger van to and from assigned off-campus locations within Westminster. Break Shuttle responsibilities consist of transporting student passengers in an 11-passenger van to and from Baltimore-Washington International Thurgood Marshall Airport and BWI Amtrak Station. Requirements: A valid Class C driver's license for at least six years and point-free driving record for at least three years (CDL not required) Availability to work Monday thru Saturdays. Occasionally Sundays are required. Familiar with the BWI Airport, BWI Amtrak, and the local Westminster area. Demonstrate ability to drive an 11-passenger van. Ability to communicate efficiently via cell phone. Ability to communicate effectively with students and Campus Safety staff. Additional Information: McDaniel College, in compliance with federal and state laws and regulations, does not discriminate in the recruitment, admission, and employment of students, faculty, and staff in the operation of any of its educational programs and activities. McDaniel College will not tolerate any discrimination or harassment on the basis of any protected status including protective hairstyle, race, religion, color, ancestry or national origin, disability, age, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, pregnancy, military status, genetic information, marital status, veteran's status, or any other actual or perceived legally protected characteristics. Application Instructions: For a complete job description including essential responsibilities and to apply, please visit the college's employment webpage. Completed applications must include a cover letter addressing position qualifications and related experience, resume, and the names and contact information of three professional references. Review of applications will begin immediately. The position will be open until filled. Please click the Apply Now button below to begin your application. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation McDaniel College 2 College Hill Westminster, MD, 21157"
