 click here to review the 2026 benefits guidebook and click here to view 2026 premium rates . Click here to see how McDaniel College employees impact the lives of students. Job Description: This position is responsible for assisting students who need academic mentorship. This assistance involves the implementation of an academic plan that targets the student's academic, social, and emotional wellbeing. The GA reports directly to the Director of the Student Accessibility and Support Services Office. This position is a part-time position (8-24 hours per week). The Graduate Assistant works 8 hours a week in SASS to receive tuition remission for one 3 credit graduate course; more hours (8.75) required for Counselor Education degree.  SASS will compensate up to three 3-credit graduate courses per semester. Specific Responsibilities: Hold weekly appointments with Academic Skills Program (ASP) and/or Basic Program students assisting with: Study skills Time management/organizational skills Written assignments Test preparation Academic project support Assist in exam administration Serve as a proctor Read tests Scribe tests/essays for students Assure testing procedures are strictly followed Assure the school honor code is strictly adhered to Monitor testing center and student work room Assist in mid-term and final testing week preparation Deliver tests Perform other duties as assigned Assist with management of tutoring and note taking systems Meet weekly with the Director Assist Accommodations Administrative Assistant at front desk. Provide front desk coverage when requested. Create SASS display board and flyers Facilitate evening study sessions Perform other duties as assigned by supervisor Requirements: Enrolled in a graduate program at McDaniel College. Have a strong work ethic. Demonstrated team-building management skills. Experienced working with diverse constituencies. Excellent oral and written communications skills. Availability to work daytime and/or evenings. Additional Information: McDaniel College, in compliance with federal and state laws and regulations, does not discriminate in the recruitment, admission, and employment of students, faculty, and staff in the operation of any of its educational programs and activities. McDaniel College will not tolerate any discrimination or harassment on the basis of any protected status including protective hairstyle, race, religion, color, ancestry or national origin, disability, age, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, pregnancy, military status, genetic information, marital status, veteran's status, or any other actual or perceived legally protected characteristics. Application Instructions: Completed applications must include a cover letter addressing position qualifications and related experience, resume, and the names and contact information of three professional references. Review of applications will begin immediately. The position will be open until filled. Please click the Apply Now button below to begin your application. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation McDaniel College 2 College Hill Westminster, MD, 21157"
